| Layer | Metric | Threshold (verbatim) | Judged by | Trade-off direction |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| stage2 (cell) | energy_density_wh_kg | ≥ 327.18 Wh/kg | calc-energy output | ED ↑ ↔ plating resistance ↓ (N/P↑, σ_e↑ help plating but N/P↑ costs ED); ED ↑ ↔ lowT ↑ (thin electrodes help lowT, cost ED) |
| stage2 | sei_100cyc_nm | ≤ 500 | aging 100cyc output (bridge) | k_sei ↓ has no ED cost |
| stage2 | sei_500cyc_nm | ≤ 550 | aging 500cyc output (bridge) | k_sei ↓ has no ED cost |
| stage2 | lowT_retention_pct | ≥ 90% | lowT/1C ratio (bridge) | transport formulation ↑ helps lowT and plating, no ED cost |
| stage3 (safety) | plated | false | 4C charge 45°C anode_potential_v | mitigated by σ_e↑, r_neg↓, N/P↑, porosity↑ |

Priority: all hard contracts; expected conflicts ED vs (N/P, electrode thickness).

## 2. Baseline parameter facts (dumped, Chen2020)
- 5 Ah nominal; area 0.1027 m²; pos 75.6 μm/por 0.335/ρ 3262 (active 0.665); neg 85.2 μm/por 0.25/ρ 1657 (active 0.75); sep 12 μm/por 0.47/ρ 397; CC 16 μm Al + 12 μm Cu; particle radii 5.22/5.86 μm.
- Estimated layer mass: pos 0.164, neg 0.106, Al 0.043, Cu 0.108, sep 0.0025 kg/m² → total ≈ 0.423 kg/m² → ≈ 43.5 g cell.
- SEI: k_sei 1e-12 m/s; j_SEI 1.5e-7 A/m²; electrolyte σ/D = Nyman2008 functions (T-dependent); t⁺ 0.2594.
- Initial state cathode 27% lithiated → known first-cycle capacity artifact (SKILL anti-pattern); ED computed mechanically from discharge output; ceiling assessment will quantify.

## 3. Candidate strategy
- R1: baseline full sweep → gap vector.
