- Lever ladder per gap (ordered):
  - ED: thinner CC (Al 16→10 μm, Cu 12→8 μm — manufacturing-feasible), thinner separator 12→8 μm? (must stay >0; commercial separators 7-25 μm), thicker electrodes (diminishing returns), N/P rebalance; if ceiling < 327.18 → escalate to Stage 2 (system switch: OKane2022 SiOx higher negative capacity; or custom).
  - Plating@4C: (1) negative particle radius ↓ (surface area ↑), (2) electrolyte σ ↑ (formulation), (3) negative porosity ↑ / thickness ↑ (N/P), (4) t⁺ ↑.
  - lowT: (1) electrolyte σ/D formulation overrides with weak T-dependence (literature-based values), (2) porosity ↑, (3) thinner electrodes, (4) particle radius ↓ (kinetics).
  - SEI: (1) anode coating candidate (inorganic Al2O3 ALD type, funnel skipped) → k_sei ↓; (2) j_SEI ↓ (electron-migration-limited branch).
- Rounds 2-6: targeted variants; batch log-evaluate each round.

## 4. Budget allocation
R1 baseline sweep; R2-4 architecture+transport variants; R5 SEI kinetics; R6 final verification sweep of the best design; real_compute=false (no true DFT/MD).

## 5. Risk & fallback
- lowT retention may hit model limits (SPMe at 253 K; electrolyte functions T-dependence) → three-strike questioning: system reachability / task boundary (freedoms all adjustable — already widest) / metric reachability → negative-result close with "reachable if X relaxed" if truly unreachable.
